Re-arm the CGEventTap when macOS disables it.

Upstream calls tap_enable() once at startup and never again. macOS switches an
active tap off whenever the callback is slow to return (kCGEventTapDisabledByTimeout)
or the user disables input; upstream's callback drops those events into its catch-all
arm, so the tap stays dead and every hotkey silently stops working until rustcast is
restarted. This stores the tap port on CallbackData so the callback can re-enable it.

Not submitted upstream yet -- see MystikoLab/rustcast, no issue filed for this.

